        <div id="post-700" class="post-700 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-net category-nhibernate">

          <div class="post-header">
           <h3 class="post-title"><a href="http://cromwellhaus.com/2007/12/nhibernate-query-generator-installer-for-visual-studio-2008/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link: NHibernate Query Generator Installer for Visual Studio 2008">NHibernate Query Generator Installer for Visual Studio 2008</a></h3>
           <p class="post-date">
            <span class="month">Dec</span>
            <span class="day">7</span>
           </p>
           <p class="post-author">
            <span class="info">Posted by <a href="http://cromwellhaus.com/author/cromwellryan/" title="Posts by cromwellryan ">cromwellryan</a> in <a href="http://cromwellhaus.com/category/net/" title="View all posts in .Net" rel="category tag">.Net</a>, <a href="http://cromwellhaus.com/category/nhibernate/" title="View all posts in NHibernate" rel="category tag">NHibernate</a> | <a href="http://cromwellhaus.com/2007/12/nhibernate-query-generator-installer-for-visual-studio-2008/#respond" class="comments"  title="Comment on NHibernate Query Generator Installer for Visual Studio 2008"><span class="dsq-postid" rel="700 /blogs/ryanc/archive/2007/12/07/nhibernate-query-generator-installer-for-visual-studio-2008.aspx">No Comments</span></a>              </span>
           </p>
          </div>

          <div class="post-content clearfix">
          <p>I posted recently a manual .reg file for adding the NHibernate Query Generator custom tool to Visual Studio 2008.&nbsp; I just sent Ayende an update to the .Setup Product.wxs, a WiX file, which adds a new fixture specifically for 2008.&nbsp; If you are interested in building the installer and running the trunk of NHQG, below [...]</p>

